      "title": "Frame, Rocker & Floor Rust — the Scout's Defining Weak Point",
      "howToFix": "Restorers do a body-off (frame-off) restoration: media-blast the frame, cut out and weld in new boxing/crossmember sections, then coat inside and out and inject cavity wax (e.g. Fluid Film / wax-oil) into the boxed rails to stop it returning. Reproduction steel — full floor pans, rocker/rocker-cap panels, cab corners, rear quarters and tailgate skins (Anything Scout, IH Parts America, C2C Fabrication) — replaces rotted shemetal rather than skim-filling it. Reinstall on fresh polyurethane body-mount bushings. Done once properly, the cavity wax + sealed seams is what keeps it from rotting again.",
