      "title": "Heat-Soaked Starter Solenoid — No Hot-Restart",
      "howToFix": "The bulletproof fix restorers use is a remote starter relay kit: a Ford-style or cube relay mounted away from exhaust heat that takes a tiny trigger current from the worn ignition switch and switches full battery current straight to the solenoid (kits from ScoutParts/IH Parts America). This restores strong hot cranking and takes the load off the old switch. Pair it with refreshed/upsized battery and starter cables and re-fit the factory exhaust-to-starter heat shield. Many also fit a modern gear-reduction mini-starter that tolerates heat far better.",
