      "title": "Rusted/Pinholed Steel Fuel Tank & Failing Sending Unit",
      "howToFix": "Restorers stop patching and fit a modern polyethylene replacement tank (e.g. Raybuck 19-gal poly tank for 72-80 Scout II) — it physically can't rust again — installed with new straps, filler hose, and a fresh sending unit and gasket at the same time (the standard 'do them together' rule). Add an inline filter and, on builds running EFI/LS swaps, an EMS/in-tank pump provision. Result is reliable fuel delivery and an accurate, repaired gauge.",
