      "title": "Weak Stock Charging System (Low-Output Alternator/Generator)",
      "howToFix": "The community upgrade is a one-wire/plug-in high-output alternator — a GM CS130 bolts in as a near plug-and-play swap, and 140-160 amp units are sold specifically for Scouts (Anything Scout, IH Parts America). On a Scout 80/800 still running a generator, restorers do the full generator-to-alternator conversion. The critical, often-skipped step: run a new heavy-gauge charge wire from the alternator output to the battery (the original wiring can't carry the higher output). Pair with a refreshed ground strap set to cure the dim-light/dead-light gremlins.",
