      "title": "Frame Fatigue & Cracking at the Steering-Box Mount",
      "howToFix": "The proven fix is a bolt-on steering-box-to-frame brace (the 'Straight Steer' brace and similar reinforcement plates from IH Parts America / Anything Scout, for 1971-80 Scout II/Terra/Traveler). It ties the box to a second frame location, stiffening the rail so it stops flexing — tightening up the wander AND stopping the fatigue cracking. On trucks already cracked, restorers weld in a reinforcement/boxing plate first, then add the brace. Considered mandatory on anything running 33-inch or larger tires.",
