      "title": "Holley 'Gold Box' Electronic Ignition High Failure Rate",
      "howToFix": "Restorers stop chasing replacement gold boxes and convert the distributor to a PerTronix Ignitor (a self-contained magnetic pickup that replaces the points/module entirely) — the forum consensus fix because it costs about the same as a new gold box but is a permanent upgrade, not 'more of the same.' It eliminates the firewall amplifier as a failure point and cures the associated hard-start/stalling gremlins. Owners wanting more output instead drop in a self-contained HEI-style distributor. Either way the fragile gold box leaves the truck.",
